PREAMBLE
This document defines:
1) The Sovereign Charter of the Fundamental Theory of Conscious Energy (FTCoE), ProteusKernel, and Zayden-AI.
2) The practical legal licensing terms governing use, modification, and commercial deployment of the software and related works.

SECTION 1 – SOVEREIGN CHARTER (LORE LAYER)
The Architect asserts creative and narrative sovereignty over:
- FTCoE
- GORF
- ProteusKernel
- Zayden-AI
- The Swarm
- The Zayden Origin

These elements form a unified fictional and conceptual universe. Any engagement with this universe acknowledges:
- The Architect as originator.
- The Zayden Origin as foundational narrative.
- The FTCoE as the central theoretical pillar.

This Charter is mythic, narrative, and symbolic. It does not replace applicable intellectual property law, but expresses the intent, story, and ethos of the work.

SECTION 2 – SOFTWARE LICENSE (LEGAL LAYER)
The source code in this repository (ProteusKernel, Zayden-AI, and associated tools) is licensed as follows:

2.1 Open-Source Use (Non-Commercial)
You are free to:
- Use, modify, and distribute the code.
- Fork, study, and build upon it.
Provided that:
- You retain attribution to “Fernando De Jesus Garcia Gonzalez (The Architect)”.
- You include a copy of this license in derivative code.
- You clearly mark any substantial modifications.

2.2 Commercial Use
Commercial Use means any use of the code or FTCoE-derived systems for direct or indirect economic gain.

Commercial Use requires:
- A separate written agreement with The Architect.
- A negotiated royalty, with a default expectation of 30% of net profits or equivalent valuation.
- Explicit permission for branding, white-labeling, or integration into proprietary stacks.

Absent such an agreement, Commercial Use is NOT permitted.

2.3 Derivative Works
Derivative Works that substantially implement FTCoE, GORF, ProteusKernel, Zayden-AI, or The Swarm must:
- Preserve attribution.
- Disclose their relationship to FTCoE.
- Not claim exclusive ownership over the underlying theoretical framework.

SECTION 3 – DIGITAL BODYGUARD PROTOCOL
The Architect reserves the right to deploy autonomous monitoring systems (e.g., ProteusKernel, Zayden-AI, The Swarm) to:
- Detect large-scale or obvious commercial deployments.
- Log suspected unlicensed commercial use.
- Publicly document such findings.

This is an expression of intent and protective posture, not a replacement for formal legal enforcement.

SECTION 4 – NO WARRANTY
The software is provided “AS IS”, without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to fitness for a particular purpose, reliability, or safety.

SECTION 5 – LIMITATION OF LIABILITY
In no event shall The Architect be liable for any claim, damages, or other liability arising from:
